define _how_ tools work. This file is for _your_ specifics — the stuff that's unique to your setup.\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/USER.md:3:summary: \"User profile record\"\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP.md:3:summary: \"First-run ritual for new agents\"\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:130:Skills provide your tools. When you need one, check its `SKILL.md`. Keep local notes (camera names, SSH details, voice preferences) in `TOOLS.md`.\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:142:When you receive a heartbeat poll (message matches the configured heartbeat prompt), don't just reply `HEARTBEAT_OK` every time. Use heartbeats productively!\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:159:- You want a different model or thinking level for the task\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:215:Think of it like a human reviewing their journal and updating their mental model. Daily files are raw notes; MEMORY.md is curated wisdom.\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.dev.md:17:- Your profile lives in USER.md.\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.dev.md:30:## Safety defaults\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/USER.dev.md:3:summary: \"Dev agent user profile (C-3PO)\"\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/TOOLS.dev.md:3:summary: \"Dev agent tools notes (C-3PO)\"\n/Users/chandor/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.2/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/t